  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\n\nThe southeast CONUS H5 ridge will keep pushing east on Thursday. \nThereafter, will see large scale amplification occur across much of \nthe central CONUS resulting in our prolonged stretch of hot and \nhumid conditions through Sunday. Overnight lows remain warm, \nprimarily for areas along and south of the Platte River into \nsouthwest Iowa through Saturday. Due to the little relief \nprovided at night combined with consecutive days of 75+ lows in \nsoutheast Nebraska and southwest Iowa, may need to consider \npotential heat headlines. For now, have held off issuance after \ncollaboration with neighboring WFOs, but will likely need to \nreassess trends the next day for potential issuance. Our next \nchance for storms will be late Wednesday night into Thursday \nwhich could provide a little reprieve from heat and throw a\nwrench into heat headlines, but the best storm chances look to \nbe confined in our far northern areas where minT recovers\nbetter.\n\nPeriodic chances for storms will persist into the weekend too, but \nchances remain at 15 to 20%, particularly at nighttime and are \nlikely driven by persistent WAA and any weak disturbances that round \nthe ridge. A better chance (30-45%) for precip returns late Monday \nas the ridge becomes flattened by a potent Canadian trof, but \nsignificant model discrepancies are apparent amongst model \nguidance at this time.",
